  "audio": "public/audio/railway-ballast.wav",
  "duration": 23.195,
  "tempo": 1.12,
  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "Train tracks sit on a bed of sharp,",
      "start": 0.106,
      "end": 1.624
    },
    {
      "text": "angular gravel,",
      "start": 1.928,
      "end": 2.607
    },
    {
      "text": "and it is there on purpose.",
      "start": 2.852,
      "end": 3.924
    },
    {
      "text": "A loaded train puts enormous weight onto a",
      "start": 4.226,
      "end": 6.137
    },
    {
      "text": "thin steel rail,",
      "start": 6.227,
      "end": 6.995
    },
    {
      "text": "and the stones spread that load sideways so",
      "start": 7.223,
      "end": 9.259
    },
    {
      "text": "the ground underneath does not sink.",
      "start": 9.295,
      "end": 10.724
    },
    {
      "text": "Because they are angular rather than rounded,",
      "start": 10.976,
      "end": 12.781
    },
    {
      "text": "they lock against each other and stop the track",
      "start": 13.039,
      "end": 14.825
    },
    {
      "text": "creeping out of line.",
      "start": 14.896,
      "end": 15.683
    },
    {
      "text": "Rain drains through the gaps instead of turning",
      "start": 16.04,
      "end": 17.719
    },
    {
      "text": "the bed to mud.",
      "start": 17.773,
      "end": 18.47
    },
    {
      "text": "And the layer soaks up vibration,",
      "start": 18.755,
      "end": 20.255
    },
    {
      "text": "which is why a passing train shakes the ground",
      "start": 20.505,
      "end": 22.184
    },
    {
      "text": "less than it should.",
      "start": 22.273,
      "end": 22.952
    }
  ],
